                <pb facs="0447" n="435" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg435"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.105A/11–2944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-29T17:00:00-04:00">November 29,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>697. British Embassy here has again raised question of possibility of Schwarzkopf
                    assuming jurisdiction over Iranian police. Imminent arrival in Tehran of Major
                    Preston after having discussed this and other <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >gendarmerie</hi> problems in Washington offers good opportunity to discuss
                    question with Schwarzkopf with idea of arriving at a definite decision. Dept has
                    no desire to put pressure on Iranian Government to accept Schwarzkopf or any
                    other American as police adviser. However, it is understood that Iranian
                    Government has already made tentative approach to Schwarzkopf on subject so that
                    renewal of the discussions at Schwarzkopf’s instance could not be considered as
                    pressure from this end. Please discuss with Schwarzkopf and with Iranian
                    Government if you deem advisable and give Dept benefit of your recommendations.
                    You may inform Schwarzkopf that Dept will support with War his recommendations
                    for increase in staff to meet the added work and responsibility entailed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
